# SwiftUI Views

- Extract subviews as `private var subview: some View` or separate `private struct`s; keep `body` a thin composition of them.
- Never put business logic or heavy computation inside `body` — delegate to the ViewModel or a helper.
- Scope property wrappers to their real lifetime:
  - `@State` — local, view-owned value state.
  - `@StateObject` — reference type the view creates and owns.
  - `@ObservedObject` — reference type injected from outside.
  - `@EnvironmentObject` — app-wide shared state.
- Add a `#Preview` for every new view.
- Naming: `<Name>View`.
